Dialogue: 0,0:00:34.54,0:00:37.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It feels great! Come on down!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:38.82,0:00:40.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Go on, she's calling you.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:40.98,0:00:41.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No she's not.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:41.99,0:00:45.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes, she is.\NSee? She's looking at you.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:45.08,0:00:46.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Buzz off, will you?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:50.75,0:00:53.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Aw, he beat you to the punch.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:53.04,0:00:54.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yay!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:55.43,0:00:56.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This is dumb.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:56.52,0:00:57.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:57.28,0:01:00.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This is only fun for people whose sense of danger is dulled.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:01.40,0:01:04.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's not as though anything changes once you jump.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:05.47,0:01:07.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah, this is the sort of thing that I—
Dialogue: 0,0:01:06.71,0:01:07.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Just jump already!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:11.90,0:01:12.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh, crap!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:12.69,0:01:13.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,For the love of...
Dialogue: 0,0:01:13.56,0:01:14.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Wait.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:13.56,0:01:15.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No, this is gonna be bad.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:32.30,0:01:33.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Huh?\NWhat was that?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:33.58,0:01:36.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That was our world, wasn't it?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:36.53,0:01:37.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Then did we just go home?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:42.01,0:01:45.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're amazing, you know that?\NYour talents can achieve anything.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:45.35,0:01:46.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I wouldn't go that far.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:47.33,0:01:51.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This just comes in handy, is all—\Nit's not the kind of power that changes the world.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:51.94,0:01:52.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't you think?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:54.01,0:01:57.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Still, this world's so unfair, isn't it?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:57.07,0:02:00.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There's someone on this island who doesn't need to compensate the others.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:00.62,0:02:04.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There are definitely those in the world\Nwho are chosen to get special treatment.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:05.77,0:02:07.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How's the plan coming along?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:07.15,0:02:11.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh, yeah...
Dialogue: 0,0:02:07.15,0:02:13.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Things are starting to come together,\N but some key elements still remain unclear.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:13.93,0:02:14.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It'll be fine.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:15.57,0:02:18.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Someone will eventually show up to save us.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:23.17,0:02:25.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mm, this is good!\NToo spicy.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:25.97,0:02:27.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hey, pass the water.\NYou know,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:27.97,0:02:30.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,we could probably get back home with his power, couldn't we?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:30.98,0:02:33.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We made it home earlier for a moment.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:33.65,0:02:36.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But I'm not even sure if it is my power.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:36.27,0:02:39.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why not? You gotta take responsibility for your actions.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:39.02,0:02:41.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You did that thing, didn't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:41.03,0:02:42.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What do you call it, warping?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:44.52,0:02:47.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Even Rajdhani says so. Go on, do it.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:48.42,0:02:50.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I really don't know if it was me.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:50.37,0:02:53.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It doesn't feel like I did anything.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:53.02,0:02:56.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ugh, man, you really are useless.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:56.37,0:02:59.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're seriously dragging everyone down.\NPull it together, asshole.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:02.87,0:03:06.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Then again, was that really {\i1}our {\i0}world?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:02.87,0:03:06.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hmm, I'm not sure.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:07.35,0:03:09.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It wasn't actually the "light," for the record.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:10.58,0:03:12.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Should we have Rajdhani look into it tomorrow?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:14.08,0:03:15.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That monkey...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:16.16,0:03:17.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Special delivery!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:17.72,0:03:19.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hey, having dinner together?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:31.41,0:03:33.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He's still pissed.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:33.62,0:03:37.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I said I was sorry, but he just can't seem to let it go.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:38.13,0:03:39.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Such a child.{I'd probably still be pissed if someone hit me with a baseball bat. - L}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:41.92,0:03:44.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Is carrying that stuff here your job?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:44.53,0:03:48.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Just use your power. What is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:47.66,0:03:51.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh, it's not some fancy kind of power.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:51.37,0:03:54.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah... I'd rather not say what it is.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:54.77,0:03:55.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh hey, Nagara,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:55.27,0:03:58.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,wanna play a little baseball together again sometime?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:58.09,0:04:00.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Huh? Where's this coming from?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:00.75,0:04:03.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I have to practice once in a while, or I'll get rusty.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:03.41,0:04:05.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Come on, join me.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:05.13,0:04:07.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Wow, this is a surprise. You were in the baseball club?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:07.79,0:04:09.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I don't remember.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:09.03,0:04:11.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Are you for real? I'll never forget it!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:11.86,0:04:15.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,During our last{ little league} tournament,\Nyour three consecutive errors cost us the game!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:15.88,0:04:17.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I-Is that right?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:17.77,0:04:20.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If it weren't for that, we could have gone to Nationals!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:22.42,0:04:24.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hey, you okay?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:25.93,0:04:28.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ace is around, right?\NWhy don't you play with him?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:28.97,0:04:32.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No can do. You know how much he hates to practice.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:32.59,0:04:35.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Besides, lately he's been too busy with his girlfriend.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:35.91,0:04:37.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh yeah, {\i1}her{\i0}.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:38.12,0:04:40.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Must be nice to be popular.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:41.06,0:04:43.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hey, any of you heard what Ace's power is?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:43.94,0:04:45.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I haven't.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:45.31,0:04:46.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:46.10,0:04:48.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Apparently it's "Sweetwater."
Dialogue: 0,0:04:48.16,0:04:49.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Huh? What does that do?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:49.83,0:04:50.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Exactly that.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:50.95,0:04:55.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Supposedly, he can make any water drinkable.{This girl is severely underestimating the severity of a looming water crisis}\NWhat a riot!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:55.38,0:05:00.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,For all that big talk, he gets to drink muddy water and say it's yummy.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:00.57,0:05:04.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Say, if you're asking for baseball practice,\Ndoes that mean you have a place where you can play?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:04.34,0:05:08.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,As a matter of fact,\NI made a baseball diamond not far from here.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:08.36,0:05:09.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Whoa, did you?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:09.78,0:05:10.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:10.74,0:05:11.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's amazing.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:20.60,0:05:23.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Huh? What's that, monkeys?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:27.89,0:05:29.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That was awesome, transfer kid!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:29.65,0:05:30.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:30.11,0:05:33.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Nobody's beaten the Rock Monster since Steroid!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:33.49,0:05:34.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Huh? Who's that?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:34.95,0:05:36.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Steroid Monkey!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:36.88,0:05:40.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Eight-time record-setter for\Nhome runs in the Monkey League!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:40.05,0:05:42.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Wait, what's the Monkey League?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:42.08,0:05:44.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Huh? You don't know?!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:44.51,0:05:49.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh, right, you can't see them, huh? Sorry 'bout that.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:52.53,0:05:53.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Monkey League—
Dialogue: 0,0:05:54.38,0:05:57.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's a baseball league here in the world of Monkey Mountain,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:57.32,0:06:00.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,played by the great monkeys,\Nwhich started when the first ball and bat
Dialogue: 0,0:06:00.60,0:06:03.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and the rules of the game were handed down to them.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:04.56,0:06:10.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}In the Monkey League, a number of great players arose from among the nameless masses,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:10.57,0:06:12.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}who all bore the same appearances.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:12.66,0:06:16.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}The legendary home run king,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:12.66,0:06:19.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}who hit an unprecedented, record-breaking 80 home runs in one year, Steroid Monkey!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:19.82,0:06:24.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}Toppling the god of batting,\NMonkey River's career batting average
Dialogue: 0,0:06:19.82,0:06:27.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}by two thousandths,\N the miracle hitting machine, Upper Monkey!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:27.57,0:06:31.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}The greatest catcher of the Bigfoot era, Mister Monkey,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:31.08,0:06:34.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}who as a manager would go on to break the record for most league wins,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:34.87,0:06:37.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}with a legendary ten-season-long streak!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:37.66,0:06:40.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Then came the golden age of the M-League.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:40.39,0:06:44.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,A miracle monkey came along and dethroned those previous legends one by one.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:44.03,0:06:46.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The monster, Monkey Blue!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:46.55,0:06:49.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This maverick of the league was the only one with blue hair,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:49.43,0:06:52.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,who, despite weathering ugly\Ndiscrimination and crafty persecution,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:52.59,0:06:56.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,triumphed with overwhelming talent,\Nto ultimately become a hero,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:56.27,0:06:58.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and a symbol of hope for the monkeys!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:59.35,0:07:02.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Despite being a rookie,\NBlue put the brakes to the king, Steroid Monkey!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:02.45,0:07:05.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Breaking his bat along with his heart,\NBlue drove him to retirement.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:05.97,0:07:09.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Then, with his mighty pitching arm, Blue led his underdog team Monkey and Club to victory,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:09.47,0:07:12.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,preventing Bigfoot's championship streak from reaching 11.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:12.03,0:07:16.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The public accepted this new hair color,\Nand there was no doubt in anybody's mind
Dialogue: 0,0:07:16.04,0:07:18.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,that the era of Monkey Blue had begun!\NBut then...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:18.93,0:07:25.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,a great tragedy shook the sport,\Nwhen a near-perfect game was foiled,\Nand a monkey was killed in the diamond!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:25.59,0:07:27.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I wanna see them! I wanna see the monkeys!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:27.77,0:07:29.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Huh? {\i1}That's{\i0} your takeaway?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:29.44,0:07:31.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I want to see the monkeys, too!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:31.13,0:07:32.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I know, right? Monkeys! Monkeys!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:32.85,0:07:33.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I want my own pet monkey!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:34.13,0:07:35.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Where can we see them?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:37.41,0:07:38.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Right here.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:38.60,0:07:40.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Huh? Where?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:40.09,0:07:41.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Like I said, here.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:41.51,0:07:43.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Uh, {\i1}here{\i0}?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:43.31,0:07:43.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:44.35,0:07:48.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Right here.\NBut it's not like you can just wait around and see them.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:48.61,0:07:51.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You need to use a certain piece of gear.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:51.66,0:07:52.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Gear?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:52.51,0:07:53.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What kind of gear?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:54.29,0:07:55.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh, the monkeys?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:55.80,0:07:59.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's right. You have to use one of these to see the monkeys.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:00.35,0:08:02.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,A Monkey Getter. Wanna borrow it?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:04.37,0:08:04.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:05.15,0:08:07.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,[No! No way in hell!]
Dialogue: 0,0:08:10.39,0:08:12.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hey, if money's the problem, I got you covered. See?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:12.94,0:08:16.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's not about the money. She just doesn't like you.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:16.57,0:08:21.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Damn her. If we had that thing,\Nwe could see the monkeys!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:21.07,0:08:24.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What do we do? Steal it?\NThreaten them? Beat them? Trick them?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:24.96,0:08:26.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Take it easy.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:24.96,0:08:27.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So what do we do?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:27.65,0:08:31.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hey, how do you all even know about the monkeys in the first place?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:31.81,0:08:35.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We were helping Cap with some baseball practice,\Nand he told us about them.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:35.77,0:08:36.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:36.59,0:08:37.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:37.63,0:08:39.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Can you really see monkeys with that thing?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:39.63,0:08:41.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Huh? You don't believe me?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:41.61,0:08:44.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,N-No, it's not that.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:44.45,0:08:48.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I get what you mean, though.\NIt just looks like a regular flashlight, doesn't it?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:48.77,0:08:53.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But if you shine it on yourself like this,\Nyou become able to see the monkeys.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:53.65,0:08:56.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Or maybe more precisely,\Nthe world where the monkeys live.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:56.49,0:08:57.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:57.94,0:09:00.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Then again, Nagara, for you, why not?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:00.63,0:09:03.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah, for old time's sake, as former teammates.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:03.69,0:09:04.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You'll lend it to him?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:06.29,0:09:07.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How does this sound?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:07.80,0:09:09.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You've already got some practice in.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:09.59,0:09:12.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Play against me, and if you win, I'll let you borrow it.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:14.05,0:09:15.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,A one-inning game.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:15.72,0:09:20.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If any of you get a hit off one of my pitches, you win.\NWhat do you say?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:20.80,0:09:22.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Not a chance.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:22.04,0:09:23.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We'll play your game!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:24.77,0:09:26.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Heh, that's more like it.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:26.53,0:09:30.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But I'm not playing for nothing.\NI want something in return.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:30.55,0:09:32.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If {\i1}you{\i0} lose...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:36.74,0:09:38.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Huh? Hey, I don't know about that...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:38.94,0:09:39.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's settled!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:45.48,0:09:47.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Come on, you're not even close!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:47.28,0:09:49.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Stop dropping your elbow! Keep your head up!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:54.03,0:09:55.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I've got no hope of hitting against him.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:55.85,0:09:57.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Well, you could be right.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:57.71,0:09:59.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Is Ace really that good?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:59.96,0:10:01.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah, he's a prodigy.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:01.96,0:10:04.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He's already had pros come asking about him.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:04.34,0:10:06.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh, yeah? That is good.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:06.34,0:10:07.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hey!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:07.06,0:10:09.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What good is it if you're beaten before you even play?!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:09.51,0:10:12.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Play to win! If you don't believe in yourself, who will?!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:17.32,0:10:19.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I've never counted on myself for anything.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:22.17,0:10:23.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I can't...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:24.29,0:10:27.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Well, you never know what's going to happen during a game.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:27.57,0:10:29.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hope for a miracle and do your best.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:30.64,0:10:33.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,By the way, what was his condition for doing this?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:33.34,0:10:35.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh, nothing that important.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:38.12,0:10:41.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're not playing baseball with them?\NThey'd have it in the bag with you there.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:41.65,0:10:43.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm not interested in seeing monkeys.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:43.59,0:10:45.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Plus that oaf is there.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:45.44,0:10:49.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm terribly curious about this\Nmysterious flashlight, the Monkey Getter.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:49.95,0:10:53.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If something like that exists,\Nit could change my whole view of the world!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:54.49,0:10:56.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Makes no difference to me.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:56.09,0:10:59.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Once Nagara masters his power,\Nwe'll be home in no time.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:59.89,0:11:03.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I don't think it's quite that simple.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:05.74,0:11:09.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That year had been Blue's greatest season.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:09.46,0:11:11.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Every game, he pitched the full nine innings and won.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:11.68,0:11:15.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,With a league-high 32 wins posted,\Nthe team won its second consecutive title.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:15.88,0:11:17.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Then, in the final game of the season,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:17.98,0:11:22.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Blue was closing in on pitching an absolutely perfect game!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:22.54,0:11:23.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It was 16-0,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:23.69,0:11:26.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,with Monkey and Club commanding a huge lead going into the final inning.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:26.93,0:11:28.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Bottom of the 9th, two outs.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:28.37,0:11:31.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Blue had struck out 26 batters on 80 pitches,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:31.61,0:11:34.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and had gotten the last batter two strikes down in quick order!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:34.70,0:11:40.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The overflowing stadium was blanketed in electricity,\N waiting for the call of that last pitch to ring out!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:40.15,0:11:45.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,All of the monkeys there focused their intense gaze on Blue's every move!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:45.12,0:11:49.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,None of them had any doubt that this would be an absolutely perfect game!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:49.66,0:11:52.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes, there was indeed an uneasy foreboding.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:52.77,0:11:56.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In hindsight, it was clear.\NOne monkey, unaccustomed to that pressure—
Dialogue: 0,0:11:56.62,0:11:58.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,the peculiar umpire...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:58.90,0:12:00.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Then, the world went off-kilter.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:01.33,0:12:04.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The 81st pitch! Out of respect for Blue's honor,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:04.65,0:12:06.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I will say that it was by no means a careless pitch.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:06.79,0:12:08.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The world itself had slipped!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:08.77,0:12:11.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No, there is no possibility that I'm being partial to Blue!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:11.77,0:12:13.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It actually happened!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:13.34,0:12:17.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The world itself moved just a little bit! It's the truth!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:20.15,0:12:23.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The ball looked like it may have slightly missed the strike zone,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:23.55,0:12:26.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,but could be called as either a strike or a ball!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:26.11,0:12:30.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And the umpire making the call was the one monkey in that stadium—
Dialogue: 0,0:12:26.11,0:12:32.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,in that whole world—who did slip with the world!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:38.52,0:12:40.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The crowd rose to their feet en masse!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:40.66,0:12:44.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They started tearing out their hair,\Nand stamping their feet with all their might!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:44.04,0:12:46.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They broke out in boos! Tremendous booing!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:46.29,0:12:48.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The umpire firmly refused requests to check the video replay.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:50.07,0:12:51.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Blue was visibly dissatisfied, and charged the umpire!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:51.61,0:12:52.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,"That was a strike!"
Dialogue: 0,0:12:53.57,0:12:55.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The umpire quietly shook his head.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:55.52,0:12:56.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,"Hey, are you nuts?!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:56.80,0:12:59.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That pitch would have sealed an absolutely perfect game!"
Dialogue: 0,0:13:00.15,0:13:02.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The umpire firmly replied, "I am aware."
Dialogue: 0,0:13:02.77,0:13:04.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,"No, you don't get it!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:04.14,0:13:06.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why didn't you call that ball a strike?!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:06.61,0:13:08.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The outcome of the game is already decided!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:08.72,0:13:12.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,On top of that, this game is a throwaway anyhow!\NThe batter is dispirited!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:12.48,0:13:16.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So how come, when it didn't matter if you called that pitch a strike or a ball,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:16.29,0:13:17.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,did you not call it a strike?!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:17.89,0:13:19.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What was the point of that?!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:19.93,0:13:24.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Moreover, do you not hear the cheers of hope and anticipation from the crowd?!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:24.00,0:13:27.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You know that this isn't the outcome they wanted!"
Dialogue: 0,0:13:28.32,0:13:30.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,"I am aware of that, as well."
Dialogue: 0,0:13:31.37,0:13:32.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So, why did he?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:33.47,0:13:36.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,"The hopes of the crowd have no bearing on this game.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:36.83,0:13:39.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There is a stadium here, and inside it, there are rules.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:39.49,0:13:42.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No matter what the reasons may be, things should remain fair in here."
Dialogue: 0,0:13:43.99,0:13:45.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,"You're wrong!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:45.39,0:13:47.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This is a baseball show!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:47.07,0:13:50.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Everyone is pinning their hopes and dreams on me!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:50.02,0:13:52.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm carrying the weight of the whole Monkey League!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:52.99,0:13:55.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Right now, as far as this place goes, {\i1}I{\i0} am the rules!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:56.35,0:13:58.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Now, reverse your decision!"
Dialogue: 0,0:13:58.17,0:14:01.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Blue's huge hands were trembling.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:01.04,0:14:02.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,"I cannot do that."
Dialogue: 0,0:14:03.97,0:14:05.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The umpire was utterly unflinching.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:05.17,0:14:08.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,"Right now, as far as this place is concerned, {\i1}I{\i0} am the rules."
Dialogue: 0,0:14:09.89,0:14:13.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Blue knew the truth as well.\NThe replay was shown on the big screen.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:14.52,0:14:20.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The fact was, due to the world slipping,\Nthe ball had missed the strike zone by no more than a micron!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:20.77,0:14:24.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But Blue could not accept that decision.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:25.33,0:14:28.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,When play resumed,\NBlue threw the ball at the exact same speed,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:28.48,0:14:33.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,on the exact same course as that 81st pitch,\Nthree more times.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:33.15,0:14:34.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,"Ball four!"
Dialogue: 0,0:14:35.27,0:14:38.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Spiking his glove into the mound, Blue walked off the game.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:38.02,0:14:41.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This incited the stirred-up spectators to begin rioting!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:41.87,0:14:44.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,As the crowd rushed onto the field, they all charged at the umpire!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:46.29,0:14:49.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,As the terrified batter looked on,\Nthe umpire had his head beaten in,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:49.65,0:14:52.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and the rioting crowd tore him apart.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:52.99,0:14:56.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,His thin, scruffy body had its flesh and blood trodden on,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:56.55,0:14:59.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,spat upon, dishonored, and breathed its last.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:04.31,0:15:06.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The monkey died.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:06.73,0:15:08.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,All over a game of baseball.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:09.10,0:15:13.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Blue had taken on all of their hopes for that one pitch.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:13.01,0:15:14.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What an amazing monkey.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:14.58,0:15:17.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's for sure. Blue was the best pitcher ever.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:17.82,0:15:19.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No, I meant the umpire.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:19.70,0:15:20.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:22.71,0:15:25.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He prevailed against the whole world.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:25.46,0:15:26.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're making too much of it.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:26.94,0:15:28.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Nagara, don't you feel anything?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:30.67,0:15:31.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't you feel angry?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:35.95,0:15:37.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I don't know.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:44.33,0:15:47.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Strike! Batter out!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:49.31,0:15:51.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It makes sense that that monkey got killed.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:52.50,0:15:54.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,A world where the ordinary kill the genius,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:54.57,0:15:57.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,or where ignorant fools destroy talent is...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:59.81,0:16:00.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Foul!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:04.01,0:16:06.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}With that rugged, yet beautiful form,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:06.53,0:16:09.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}she'll never even see my lightning fastball.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:11.41,0:16:13.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Strike two!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:16.91,0:16:19.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Strike! Batter out!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:22.14,0:16:23.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Good luck.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:27.69,0:16:29.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Strike!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:37.49,0:16:39.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Strike two!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:41.52,0:16:44.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So, how do you like my pitching?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:44.53,0:16:48.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah, you're really good.\NI doubt there's any way I can hit that.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:48.37,0:16:50.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You just don't feel like hitting.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:50.96,0:16:52.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There's no way I could.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:58.97,0:17:00.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why am I not...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:02.51,0:17:04.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,B-Ball!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:04.05,0:17:05.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hey, watch out!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:05.78,0:17:08.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah, yeah! That was a beanball! Eject him!{I'm so glad this TL knows baseball. - L}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:08.85,0:17:10.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He is so lame!{TLC}{Huh?}{Can be read as "damn he's bad" too tbh}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:10.37,0:17:11.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He is handsome, though.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:11.94,0:17:13.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hey, you okay?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:11.94,0:17:16.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm the one who gave baseball to the monkeys.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:19.52,0:17:21.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I am special.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:22.77,0:17:27.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If you lose,\Nthen you return us to our world as soon as possible.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:27.82,0:17:32.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You can't tell me you can't do it, either.\NI heard. You're our "savior", right?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:33.13,0:17:35.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Huh? No, I'm not—
Dialogue: 0,0:17:35.64,0:17:38.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Just looking at you now makes me want to puke.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:38.69,0:17:41.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I can't believe someone like you got chosen.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:43.07,0:17:46.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This world is all messed up.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:43.07,0:17:48.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Put us back in the world where I am properly appreciated.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:48.45,0:17:51.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's what your power is for.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:51.80,0:17:53.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I don't know if I can.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:53.87,0:17:56.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Do it. Even if it kills you.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:58.68,0:18:01.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Huh? A m-monkey?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:03.11,0:18:04.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,A one-armed monkey...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:06.03,0:18:10.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How did you know he had one arm?\NCan you see the umpire?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:21.41,0:18:25.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The truth is, you wanted to be a baseball player, too, didn't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:25.70,0:18:28.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But you couldn't.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:29.08,0:18:35.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Still, you were drawn to the sometimes cruel fairness of baseball,\Nand became an umpire.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:37.65,0:18:42.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You were watching over the game from there, this whole time.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:43.70,0:18:46.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It wasn't the umpire that got killed...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:46.06,0:18:46.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:46.92,0:18:48.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It was baseball!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:48.69,0:18:50.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Huh? What are you talking—
Dialogue: 0,0:18:50.08,0:18:50.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I saw it myself.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:52.03,0:18:55.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So he {\i1}can{\i0} do it.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:56.31,0:18:57.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You scum.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:57.46,0:18:58.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't get so full of yourself.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:00.29,0:19:01.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's it.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:05.07,0:19:05.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Go!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:09.35,0:19:11.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Strike! Batter out!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:11.85,0:19:13.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ah, you idiot!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:16.77,0:19:17.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That was awesome, Nagara!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:17.75,0:19:18.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I underestimated you.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:18.91,0:19:22.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Too bad. But that was a nice swing.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:22.27,0:19:22.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Thanks.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:22.94,0:19:26.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Aw, we don't get to see any monkeys.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:26.05,0:19:26.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Here.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:26.86,0:19:28.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Thanks.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:28.05,0:19:29.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Huh? You've got something stuck to you.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:30.84,0:19:31.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:31.94,0:19:33.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What is this?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:33.16,0:19:34.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}That didn't come from my cats.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:34.61,0:19:35.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}Is it some kind of fur?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:35.89,0:19:37.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}When did it get stuck to you?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:37.40,0:19:39.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're here to cheer me up?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:39.91,0:19:42.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,[This isn't where we're supposed to be.]
Dialogue: 0,0:19:43.36,0:19:46.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I guess today's the last day of life on the island.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:46.27,0:19:47.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm going to miss it.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:47.96,0:19:49.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,R-Right...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:50.67,0:19:54.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Actually, I've been thinking of quitting baseball for a while now.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:55.80,0:20:01.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Nobody knows better than me that\NI lack the talent to play in the big leagues.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:01.60,0:20:06.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Still, we played for the fun of it a long time ago. Just like monkeys.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:06.56,0:20:12.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But before we knew it,\Nit became about whether or not we had the talent,\Nor how it would get us into college,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:12.53,0:20:15.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and that started taking up all our attention.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:16.57,0:20:21.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But then, watching those monkeys playing,\NI couldn't sit still.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:22.05,0:20:25.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}I don't know how to say it, but it was kind of like...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:25.86,0:20:29.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}I felt like, "I wanna play baseball!"
Dialogue: 0,0:20:29.07,0:20:33.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}And once I realized that, here it was—\Nthe diamond was already in place.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:33.27,0:20:38.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}Strange, isn't it? I don't have the talent for baseball,\N{\an8}but it's all I ever think about.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:40.54,0:20:42.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}That's not so strange.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:43.09,0:20:44.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's not?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:44.52,0:20:45.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:52.41,0:20:53.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Well?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:53.70,0:20:55.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Does the plan seem like it's going to work?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:55.93,0:20:58.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Who knows? But it sure is an amazing power.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:58.93,0:21:00.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We can go anywhere.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:00.41,0:21:03.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Really? It doesn't look that way to me...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:03.53,0:21:04.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,She's not lying...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:04.59,0:21:08.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,but it also may not be exactly what everyone is thinking, either.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:09.43,0:21:13.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Nagara has reached the point where he can control his warp power.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:13.02,0:21:15.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We can say goodbye to this place now.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:15.58,0:21:17.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Okay, let's go home to our own world!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:20.77,0:21:22.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Go on, do it.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:22.99,0:21:24.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,All right.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:32.02,0:21:33.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Huh? Where are we?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:33.62,0:21:35.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh, this isn't right.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:38.08,0:21:39.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This isn't it, either.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:51.27,0:21:52.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Where's the school, already?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:52.87,0:21:54.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How long until we get there?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:54.77,0:21:56.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's enough showing off.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:56.53,0:21:58.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hey, what's wrong with you?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:59.62,0:22:00.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I can't go back.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:00.89,0:22:01.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Huh?!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:01.98,0:22:04.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Not just to our world.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:04.15,0:22:06.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I can't go where I want to.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:08.38,0:22:10.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That guy really is worthless.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:10.40,0:22:12.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}Aww, are you serious?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:10.40,0:22:14.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}Well, that sucked.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:12.40,0:22:14.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}It's our fault for expecting anything.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:12.40,0:22:14.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}That's about what I figured.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:14.41,0:22:16.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That pretty well clears that up.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:16.71,0:22:20.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Nagara has the power to move to other worlds.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:21.31,0:22:23.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But he can't choose where he goes.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:23.41,0:22:28.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I mean, I can't believe this world we've been in is one that he would choose.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:30.28,0:22:33.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hey, look over there.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:36.57,0:22:38.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Huh? M-Ms. Aki?!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:39.68,0:22:40.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,A teacher?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:40.65,0:22:43.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Someone else besides us got cast away?!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:42.12,0:22:43.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,She's here to save us!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:43.37,0:22:44.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Shut up, you worms!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:56.17,0:22:58.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Playtime's over.
